From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: imx8-mipi-csi2-sam: fix s_power NULL pointer
 dereference

mipi_csis_s_power() dereferences sen_sd->ops->core->s_power without
first checking that the remote sensor subdev actually implements the
core ops structure. Modern sensor drivers such as ov5645 only
implement .video and .pad ops and leave .core unset, so
sen_sd->ops->core is NULL and the driver crashes with a NULL pointer
dereference as soon as streaming is started:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual
  address 0000000000000048
  ...
  pc : mipi_csis_s_power+0x60/0xac [imx8_mipi_csi2_sam]
  Call trace:
   mipi_csis_s_power+0x60/0xac [imx8_mipi_csi2_sam]
   mxc_isi_cap_streamon+0x13c/0x1dc [imx8_isi_capture]
   v4l_streamon+0x20/0x28

Use v4l2_subdev_call() directly, which already performs the required
NULL checks on both csis->ops->core and csis->ops->core->s_power, and
treat the optional -ENOIOCTLCMD return as success since s_power is not
mandatory.

Signed-off-by: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate NXP proprietary driver
---
 drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-mipi-csi2-sam.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-mipi-csi2-sam.c b/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-mipi-csi2-sam.c
index f08d8c9f0a7b..05e081e47b13 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-mipi-csi2-sam.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-mipi-csi2-sam.c
@@ -1086,6 +1086,7 @@ static int mipi_csis_s_power(struct v4l2_subdev *mipi_sd, int on)
 {
 	struct csi_state *state = mipi_sd_to_csi_state(mipi_sd);
 	struct v4l2_subdev *sen_sd;
+	int ret;
 
 	/* Get remote source pad subdev */
 	sen_sd = csis_get_remote_subdev(state, __func__);
@@ -1094,10 +1095,9 @@ static int mipi_csis_s_power(struct v4l2_subdev *mipi_sd, int on)
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-	if (sen_sd->ops->core->s_power)
-		return v4l2_subdev_call(sen_sd, core, s_power, on);
-	else
-		return 0;
+	ret = v4l2_subdev_call(sen_sd, core, s_power, on);
+
+	return (ret == -ENOIOCTLCMD) ? 0 : ret;
 }
 
 static int mipi_csis_s_stream(struct v4l2_subdev *mipi_sd, int enable)
-- 
2.53.0
